2186494135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494128 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494224 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494135 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494135 1077 "III" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494135 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494224 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494135 1079 #uuid "185aa277-ec0b-5b7f-9dfd-7fd410156dfc" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494135 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494140 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494176 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6 + \\frac{4 y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1$\n- **II.** $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1$\n- **III.** $y=2 x^{4} - x$" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1072 #uuid "186f19a6-4a5f-585e-b13e-b8bce737384f" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494136 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 4 x^{3} - 2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 4 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(- x^{4} - 2 x - 1\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ - 4 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}- 4 x^{3} - 2 - \\frac{4}{x} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 12 x^{3} - 2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 12 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ - 12 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}- 12 x^{3} - 2 + \\frac{4}{x} \\\\ - \\frac{4}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 x^{4} - x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8 x^{3} - 1.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ 8 x^{3} - 1 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(2 x^{4} - x\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ 8 x^{3} - 1 & \\overset{?}{=}8 x^{3} + 2 \\\\ -3 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 x^{4} - x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494142 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494202 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1077 "I" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494142 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494137 1079 #uuid "1a713518-e004-530d-9096-230f529b44ea" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494138 1080 "false" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494138 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494138 1083 #uuid "1cf34b6d-fb8d-5cff-9900-0f2e7b496e9b" 13194139535316 17