 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494206 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494155 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494210 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494155 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494155 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=e^{x} - 1$\n- **II.** $y=- e^{x}$\n- **III.** $y=- e^{- x}$" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494155 1072 #uuid "445c16a9-31b8-52c6-9989-0214ce5be143" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494155 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=e^{x} - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(e^{x} - 1\\right) \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}e^{x} - 1 \\\\ 1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=e^{x} - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- e^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- e^{x}\\right) \\\\ - e^{x} & =- e^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=- e^{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}- e^{- x} \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494130 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494196 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1077 "III" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494196 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494156 1079 #uuid "44ec42b0-3682-544b-ac01-636f3d9ba276" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494157 1080 "false" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494157 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494157 1083 #uuid "473054af-72eb-5f9d-8413-69674dad30c2" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494125 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494153 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494154 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=3 e^{x} - 2$\n- **II.** $y=-2 + 3 e^{- x}$\n- **III.** $y=3 e^{x}$" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1072 #uuid "482041dd-1ea5-59f6-ae3d-2788e211524d" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494158 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution b