original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494163 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494179 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1077 "I" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494163 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494213 1079 #uuid "de72884f-8c58-5c74-aa9c-e35bf2e4d062" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494214 1080 "false" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494214 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [17592186494214 1083 #uuid "e160878b-1ed6-563f-9b98-b398745ccaea" 13194139535316 17592186045443 true] [175